	affiliations = {Lviv Polytechnic National University, Ukraine},
	abstract = {The article identifies the main sources of financial support for the development of territorial communities in Ukraine in the context of decentralization. It is shown that financial support plays a key role in the development of territorial communities. Therefore, solving the issue of financing territorial communities in order to ensure the development of a particular territory, local financial management is of particular importance. The success of this process provides the ability to use the features of a particular area, finding different sources of financial resources, their accumulation, the efficiency of their use and distribution, creating conditions for effective implementation of economic plans and projects, solving social programs at the local level. The main sources of financial support for the development of territorial communities are identified, which include: local budget revenues, financial support of local self-government by the state, and the search for additional sources of financial resources by local authorities by using development potential in a particular area. It is established that an important place in providing financial resources to the territorial community is played by the local budget. In recent years, the reform has seen much greater participation of local governments in increasing local budget revenues. The success in this process is achieved due to improved interaction with business representatives, increasing the number of registered businesses, and, accordingly, full payment of taxes to the local budget. Although the total amount of revenues to local budgets is growing, there is a significant difference in the revenues of different territorial communities. It was found that the largest difference between the largest and smallest values of revenues of the general fund of the local budget per 1 inhabitant in territorial communities with a population of 5-10 thousand and less than 5 thousand people The analysis shows the